{"p":"/players/teams","t":"Implement teams","d":"The Teams service allows you assign players to different teams within your game.","h":"<p>You can divide players in your game into multiple teams using the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Teams\"><code>Teams</code></a> service. By <a href=\"#add-teams\">configuring</a> the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Teams\"><code>Teams</code></a> service and <a href=\"#assign-players-to-teams\">assigning teams</a>, players are automatically differentiated by their <a href=\"#/docs/characters/name-health-display\">display name</a> color, as well as their name in the default player list.</p>\n<h2>Add teams</h2>\n<p>By default, no teams are configured. To add teams:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>In the <a href=\"https://create.roblox.com/docs/studio/explorer\">Explorer</a> hierarchy, hover over the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Teams\"><code>Teams</code></a> object and click the <strong>&CirclePlus;</strong> icon to show a list of objects.</li>\n<li>Insert a new <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Team\"><code>Team</code></a> object under the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Teams\"><code>Teams</code></a> service.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" /></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Select the new <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Team\"><code>Team</code></a> object and, in the <a href=\"https://create.roblox.com/docs/studio/properties\">Properties</a> window, change the team <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Team/Team.Name\"><code>Name</code></a> and assign a unique matching <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Team/Team.TeamColor\"><code>TeamColor</code></a>. A team's name and color both appear in the game's player list.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" /></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Repeat these steps to add more teams.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Assign players to teams</h2>\n<p>By default, Roblox <strong>auto-assigns</strong> new players joining the game to the team with the fewest members, and you can still use the following steps to assign players to a specific team.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Select each <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Team\"><code>Team</code></a> object in the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Teams\"><code>Teams</code></a> service to display its properties.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Uncheck the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Team/Team.AutoAssignable\"><code>AutoAssignable</code></a> checkbox.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" /></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Assign a player to a specific team by changing their <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Player/Player.Team\"><code>Player.Team</code></a> property to the team name in the format of <code>Teams[TEAM_NAME]</code>, such as <code>Teams[\"Blue Team\"]</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Team spawn locations</h2>\n<p>You can use <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/SpawnLocation\"><code>SpawnLocation</code></a> objects to spawn players of different teams at specific locations when they join or respawn. By default, <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/SpawnLocation\"><code>SpawnLocations</code></a> are <strong>neutral</strong> and any player can spawn upon them, so you need to lock each one to the team that can occupy it using the following steps:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Using the <a href=\"https://create.roblox.com/docs/studio/explorer\">Explorer</a>, insert a new <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/SpawnLocation\"><code>SpawnLocation</code></a> into the workspace.</li>\n<li>With the new <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/SpawnLocation\"><code>SpawnLocation</code></a> selected, uncheck its <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/SpawnLocation/SpawnLocation.Neutral\"><code>Neutral</code></a> checkbox in the <a href=\"https://create.roblox.com/docs/studio/properties\">Properties</a> window.</li>\n<li>Set the spawn's <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/SpawnLocation/SpawnLocation.TeamColor\"><code>TeamColor</code></a> property to the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Team/Team.TeamColor\"><code>TeamColor</code></a> of an existing <a href=\"#add-teams\">team</a>. For example, if the intended team's <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Team/Team.TeamColor\"><code>Team.TeamColor</code></a> is <code>Lapis</code>, set the spawn's <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/SpawnLocation/SpawnLocation.TeamColor\"><code>SpawnLocation.TeamColor</code></a> to <code>Lapis</code> as well.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"gcell\" markdown=\"block\">\n     &lt;div class=\"gcell\" markdown=\"1\"&gt;\n     &lt;figure&gt;\n     &lt;img src=\"../assets/studio/properties/Team-Name-TeamColor.png\" width=\"320\" /&gt;\n     &lt;figcaption&gt;<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Team/Team.TeamColor\"><code>Team.TeamColor</code></a>&lt;/figcaption&gt;\n   &lt;/figure&gt;\n     </div>\n<pre><code> &lt;div class=\"gcell\" markdown=\"1\"&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<figure>\n     <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" />\n   <figcaption><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/SpawnLocation/SpawnLocation.TeamColor\"><code>SpawnLocation.TeamColor</code></a></figcaption>\n   </figure>\n<pre><code> &lt;/div&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"callout c-warning\">\n<p>Note that the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/SpawnLocation/SpawnLocation.TeamColor\"><code>SpawnLocation.TeamColor</code></a> property is different from <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/SpawnLocation/SpawnLocation.BrickColor\"><code>SpawnLocation.BrickColor</code></a> and <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/SpawnLocation/SpawnLocation.Color\"><code>SpawnLocation.Color</code></a> which represent the <strong>visual</strong> color of the spawn object and are not related to team functionality.</p>\n</div>","kid":{"simple":"The `Teams` service lets you split players into groups, like Red vs Blue. Each team gets a name and a color, and players on that team show that color on their name and in the player list. You can let Roblox put players on teams for you, or choose teams yourself. You can also make spawn points that only one team can use.","analogy":"It is like gym class: everyone gets a colored jersey, and each color has its own bench to start from.","keyPoints":["No teams exist at first. Add a `Team` object under the `Teams` service in the Explorer.","Give each team a `Name` and its own `TeamColor`. Both show up in the player list.","By default, new players join the team with the fewest members because `AutoAssignable` is on.","To choose teams yourself, uncheck `AutoAssignable` and set a player's `Team` property, like `Teams[\"Blue Team\"]`.","Spawn locations are neutral at first, so anyone can spawn on them.","To make a team spawn, uncheck the spawn's `Neutral` box and set its `TeamColor` to match the team, like `Lapis`.","A spawn's `TeamColor` is not the same as its `BrickColor` or `Color`, which only change how it looks."],"terms":{"Teams service":"The container in the Explorer that holds all your `Team` objects.","TeamColor":"The color that marks a team. Players, spawns, and the team itself are matched by this color, such as `Lapis`.","AutoAssignable":"A checkbox on a team. When on, Roblox can put new players on that team automatically.","SpawnLocation":"A pad where players appear when they join or respawn.","Neutral":"A spawn setting. When checked, any player can spawn there, no matter their team.","BrickColor":"The color a part looks like. It has nothing to do with which team can use a spawn."},"example":{"title":"Put players on a team by script","place":"Script in ServerScriptService (with teams named Red Team and Blue Team, AutoAssignable unchecked)","code":"local Players = game:GetService(\"Players\")\nlocal Teams = game:GetService(\"Teams\")\n\nlocal redTeam = Teams[\"Red Team\"]\nlocal blueTeam = Teams[\"Blue Team\"]\n\nPlayers.PlayerAdded:Connect(function(player)\n\t-- Put each new player on the smaller team\n\tif #redTeam:GetPlayers() <= #blueTeam:GetPlayers() then\n\t\tplayer.Team = redTeam\n\telse\n\t\tplayer.Team = blueTeam\n\tend\n\tprint(player.Name, \"joined\", player.Team.Name)\nend)","explain":["We find the two teams inside the `Teams` service by name.","When a player joins, we count how many players each team has with `GetPlayers()`.","We set `player.Team` to the smaller team. Their name color changes to match.","This only matters if you turned off `AutoAssignable`, otherwise Roblox already balances teams."]},"watchOut":["Changing a spawn's `BrickColor` and expecting it to become a team spawn. Set `TeamColor` and uncheck `Neutral` instead.","Giving two teams the same `TeamColor`. Each team needs its own unique color.","Leaving `AutoAssignable` on while also assigning teams in a script, which can put players on teams you did not expect."]}}